 **Size to the MACHINE, measured at session start, not to a remembered box (Mike, 2026-09-23).** Process-count limits (concurrent agents, idle teammates kept alive) scale with the host's RAM, and one fixed number is wrong on every box but one. Before a wide fan-out or before choosing to hold workers idle, read the host's capacity: agent-companion's `node "$AC/scripts/capacity.mjs"` once it ships (reports total/free RAM, a concurrency budget and an idle-teammate policy); until then `Get-CimInstance Win32_OperatingSystem | Select TotalVisibleMemorySize,FreePhysicalMemory` (KB) or `free -g`. Budget ~300 MB per live agent process, keep 25% of total RAM (min 4 GB) as headroom. Where the budget comfortably exceeds the planned width, idle teammates are fine; where it's tight (16 GB-class boxes), stop workers between rounds and keep concurrency low.
